        {
          "@language": "en-US",
          "@value": "This element represents a firm commitment that would otherwise not be recognized at inception and that involves only financial instruments. For example, a forward purchase contract for a loan that is not readily convertible to cash is a commitment involving only financial instruments-a loan and cash-and would not otherwise be recognized because it is not a derivative instrument."
